sentation of the damage state of the rock, from the intact rock to the rock in the residual state. These domains are a function of the cumulative deviatoric plastic strain {\gamma}^{p} and of the stress state. Each increment of the domain number defines the passage into a higher damage domain. - If the deviator is less than 70% of the peak deviator, then the material is in domain 0; - Otherwise: - If {\gamma}^{p}=0 then the material is in domain 1; 1. If 0 {\gamma}_{	ext{ult}} then the material is in domain 4. 7.4 V4: the plastification state This is an indicator internal to Code_Aster . It is equal to 0 if the Gauss point is under elastic loading or unloading, and is equal to 1 if the Gauss point is under plastic loading. 8 Detailed presentation of the algorithm An implicit formulation with respect to the criterion and an explicit formulation with respect to the flow direction are retained: the criterion must be satisfied at the end of the step, whereas the flow direction will be that computed at the beginning of the step (and therefore the value of the dilatancy will likewise be that computed at the beginning of the time step). One places oneself at a material point, and one considers that the following are given: - The strain-increment tensor \Delta \varepsilon from which one deduces \Deltae and \Delta {\varepsilon}_{
