u}_{\mathrm{eau}}=1,1{.10}^{–6}{m}^{2}/s | (see paragraph [§1.2]) | No axial effort is applied to the tube which is therefore not prestressed. The reduced frequency and damping evolutions of the first double bending mode are calculated for an average flow speed range from 0 to 8m/s , by 1m/s step . An initial reduced depreciation of the 4.8% tube is taken into account. 3.2 Mesh characteristics The total number of nodes used for the mesh is 101. The mesh cells (SEG2 type) are 100. The mesh file is in ASTER format. 3.3 Calculation steps The validation of fluid-structure coupling operators for axial flow tube beam configurations is done in two main steps. The first is to define the parameters for taking into account fluid-structure coupling with the DEFI_FLUI_STRU operator followed by the keyword FAISCEAU_AXIAL. The second is the calculation of the reduced modal frequency and damping evolutions according to the average flow speed, with the CALC_FLUI_STRU operator and the implementation of the MEFISTEAU model. 3.4 Test values The tests are for frequency and reduced damping of the first double mode of bending of the tube, at the mean flow speed of 0m/s and 4m/s . Two types of tests are performed: 1. a comparison test with experimental measurements, 2. a test to guarantee the non-regression code. 3.4.1 Frequency of the first double bending mode 1. Comparison test with experiment, at the flow speed of 0m/s : The relative tolerance of d-difference relative to the experimental value is 0.1%. | Mode number | Experimental value | Calculated value | Ratio | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | 1 | 7 Hz | 7.000871 Hz | 1.2E-02% | | 2 | 7 Hz | 7.000871 Hz | 1.2E-02% | 3.4.2 Reduced damping of the first double bending mode 1. Comparison test with experiment at flow speed of 4 m/s: The relative tolerance of d-difference relative to the reference is 1 per cent. | Mode number | Experimental value | Calculated value | Ratio | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | 1 | 17 % | 17 % | 0,2 % | | 2 | 17 % | 1