res. The first allows to realize the calculation of a field of displacement to nodes by inversion of the structural rigidity matrix and produces the inverse by a assembled force vector, with the operators FACTORISER and RESOUDRE. The second allows the calculation of a geometric rigidity matrix using a stress field at elements, with the CALC_MATR_ELEM operator, option RIGI_GEOM. 4.4 Test values The tests are for frequency and reduced damping of the first double mode of bending of the tube, at the mean flow speed of 0m/s and 4m/s . Two types of tests are performed: 1. a comparison test with experimental measurements, 2. a test to guarantee the non-regression code. 4.4.1 Frequency of the first double bending mode 1. Comparison test with experiment, at the flow speed of 0m/s : The relative d-difference tolerance relative to the reference is 0.1 per cent. | Mode number | Experimental value | Calculated value | Ratio | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | 1 | 5,1 Hz | 5.10426 Hz | 8.4E-02% | | 2 | 5,1 Hz | 5.10426 Hz | 8.4E-02% | 4.4.2 Reduced damping of the first double bending mode 1. Comparison test with experiment, at the flow speed of 4m/s : The relative tolerance of d-difference relative to the reference is 10 per cent. | Mode number | Experimental value | Calculated value | Ratio | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | 1 | 21.10% | 21.94% | 4.00% | | 2 | 21.10% | 21.94% | 4.00% | 4.5 Remarks The reference values are those obtained by Code_Aster when the test case is returned, which allows the non-regression of the code to be verified during its evolution.

v2.02.119 SDLL119 - Beams harness under fluid-elastic axial excitation v2.02.119 SDLL119 - Beams harness under fluid-elastic axial excitation Summary A square step beam of 3	imes 3 aluminium tubes, placed in a rectangular enclosure and subjected to the action of axial water flow. The tubes contain lead pellets and are held between them at half height by piano strings. This material configuration corresponds to the experimental device of Hotta et al. [bib1] which is used to measure the reduced frequency and damping evolutions of the first mode of bending of the beam, according to the average flow speed. The purpose of this test case is to validate the MEFISTEAU R4.07.04 model's resorption to calculate the modal characteristics of a confined axial beam beam, taking into account fluid-elastic excitation. The following features to test are: - DEFI_FLUI_STRU U4.80.08 operator: definition of parameters for the consideration of fluid-elastic coupling, in the case of a configuration of the "xial flow tube beam" type (factor keyword FAISCEAU_AXIAL), - CALC_FLUI_STRU U4.80.03 operator: calculation of the evolution of modal reduced frequencies and dampings according to the average flow speed, by implementing the MEFISTEAU model. These features must be tested with the full beam representation and simplified representation. The numerical results of the Hotta et al. device simulation are validated by comparison with the experimental results. Given the relatively large uncertainties on the experimental values, the reference results for the non-regression of Code_Aster are those obtained numerically during the test case return. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry The beam tubes are hollow cylinders with the following dimensions: | length | L=1,2m | | --- | --- | | outer diameter | {\phi }_{	ext{ext}}=9,5\mathrm{mm} | | inner diameter | {\phi }_{int}=8,5\mathrm{mm} | The piano strings now the tubes between them at mid height are assimilated to cylinders full of \mathrm{2 }\mathrm{mm} d