n the test case is returned. 3 Modelling A 3.1 Modelling characteristics Each of the beam tubes is represented by 50 straight beam elements of Timoshenko (MECA_POU_D_T), supported by as many mesh cells of SEG2 type (segments to 2 nodes). A element MECA_DIS_TR is added at each end node; these elements allow the metal rods to be modeled by discrete rotational stiffeners. The elements of the tubes are assigned the characteristics of circular cross-section: | external radius | {R}_{\mathrm{ext}}=4,75{.10}^{–3}m | | | --- | --- | --- | | thickness | e={5.10}^{-4}m | (see paragraph [§1.1]) | These elements are also assigned a ELAS behavioral material: | Young's modulus | E=6,89{.10}^{10}\mathrm{Pa} | | | --- | --- | --- | | Poisson's ratio | 
