v3.03.126 SSLS126 – Flexion of a reinforced concrete slab (model GLRC_DAMAGE) with two sides: elastic beam speed v3.03.126 SSLS126 – Flexion of a reinforced concrete slab (model GLRC_DAMAGE) with two sides: elastic beam speed Summary: This test represents the calculation of a reinforced concrete slab, in bending, subjected to pressure. It allows to validate the DKTG Modelling with the GLRC_DAMAGE model for linear elastic behaviour and Q4GG Modelling with the ELAS model. The slab is in beam configuration: single supports on two opposite sides of the slab. Four modellings are performed: - Modelling A allows you to test the DKTG model with TRIA3, - Modelling B allows you to test the DKTG model with QUAD4. - Modelling C allows you to test the Q4GG model with TRIA3, - Modelling D allows you to test the Q4GG model with QUAD4. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry The square slab is l=1.8m long, h=0.12m thick, on single bilateral supports. The bending rail is parallel to the edges; it is identical on each side and in both directions ( \mathrm{dx} , \mathrm{dy} being the spacings of the irons in the x and y directions). The coating of the longitudinal irons closest to the sides is 22\mathrm{mm} . The coating of the irons in relation to the lateral edges of the 2\mathrm{cm} slab is neglected. The following table summarizes the data of the ironing. The geometric percentage of steel \mu is given for one side in a direction. | Diameter of the frames | Spacing | Steel/concrete section | grid distance/average slab area | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | \Phi =0,01	ext{m} | \mathrm{dx}=\mathrm{dy}=0,1	ext{m} | \mu =0,65	ext{} | {e}_{s}=\pm 0,038	ext{m} | {a}_{x}= rac{{A}_{x}}{{d}_{x}} , {a}_{y}= rac{{A}_{y}}{{d}_{y}} are the ferrage rates (here: {a}_{x}={a}_{y}=7,854.{10}^{-4}m ) , {A}_{x}({A}_{y}) being the cross section of an iron bar in the direction x(y) ; {e}_{z} the distance of the tablecloths to the average surface. 1.2 Material properties The characteristics of the steels are as fol