v6.01.112 SSNA112 – axisymmetric tear-out test for restraint steel-concrete study: JOINT_BA law v6.01.112 SSNA112 – axisymmetric tear-out test for restraint steel-concrete study: JOINT_BA law Summary: In this test case of mechanics the tear test carried out by La Borderie & Pijaudier- Cabot [bib1] was modelled for the purpose of studying the influence of stress state in the matrix on the mechanical properties of the interface. Geometric data and material characteristics are derived from their ratio, and the numerical results will be compared with the experimental results. Axisymmetric Modelling uses elements QUAD4 for concrete and steel, in combination with elements joint for the interface (see doc.[R3.06.09]). Concrete and steel are considered elastic to test only the nonlinearity of constitutive law of restraint steel – concrete, JOINT_BA (see document R7.01.21). Monotonous calculation is performed with forced displacements at the end of the steel bar. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry and boundary conditions Figure 1.1-a: Geometry and boundary conditions 1.2 Material properties Storage : elastic E=2.1	imes {10}^{5}\mathit{MPa} 
