v6.03.103 SSNP103 - Calculation of the nonlinear energy yield rate v6.03.103 SSNP103 - Calculation of the nonlinear energy yield rate Summary: This test is a test case in nonlinear fracture mechanics. A finished rectangular plate is considered to be cracked and subjected to traction loading. The constitutive law used is a nonlinear elastic law of the Henky von Mises type. This test case includes four modellings in \mathrm{2D} : - Model A, in flat deformations, deals with a crack pressed in pure mode 1. Only half of the plate is modelled by symmetry. - Model B, in flat deformations, deals with a crack pressed in mixed modes. The complete plate is modelled. - Modelling C takes over the geometry of Modelling A but solves the associated axisymmetric problem. It is therefore not a cracked plate here but a cracked cylinder. - Modelling D reproduces the calculation of Modelling B by adding a thermal load. - Model E reproduces the calculation of model B with linear HHO. - Modelling F, reproduces the calculation of Modelling B with quadratic HHO. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry | Length | L=400\mathit{mm} | | --- | --- | | Width | W=100\mathit{mm} | | Crack depth | a=50\mathit{mm} | 1.2 Material properties The material obeys a "non-linear" elastic constitutive law (Hencky Law) from von Linear isotropic hardening (EMAS_VMIS_LINE). The Material properties are: | Young's modulus | E=2,1	imes {10}^{5}\mathit{MPa} | | --- | --- | | Poisson's ratio | 
