tact}}}= rac{({(2/3)}^{ rac{3}{2}}-1/2)}{{(2/3)}^{ rac{3}{2}}}\approx 8,14413	ext{\%} The results obtained show that the value of {K}_{I} with contact consideration is well evaluated and higher than that obtained without contact consideration. This result underlines the importance of considering contact-related effects in numerical cracking simulations, as this example illustrates a case where the solution with interpenetration (without contact) is not conservative of point in relation to stress-intensity factors. This may prove to be not without consequence for the study of propagation, based on propagation criteria written according to stress-intensity factors.

