v6.04.204 SSNV204 – Isotropic cyclic drained compression test on sand d v6.04.204 SSNV204 – Isotropic cyclic drained compression test on sand d Summary We have the following four modellings: - Modelization A: A isotropic cyclic compression calculation is made in pure mechanics (equivalent to drained hydraulic conditions) with Hujeux's law. The calculated solutions are compared with results from elements GEFDYN finite code from the École Centrale Paris; - Modelization B: monotonous isotropic compression calculation in pure mechanics (equivalent to drained hydraulic conditions) on an orthotropic linear elastic material. Solutions are calculated by degenerating Hujeuxvers' law a linear orthotropic elastic behavior and are compared to a true orthotropic linear elastic calculation; - Modelization C: A cyclic isotropic traction calculation is made in pure mechanics (equivalent to drained hydraulic conditions) with the Hujeux law. The purpose of this Modelling is to test the traction mechanisms complementary to the Hujeux law. The calculated solutions are compared with results from elements GEFDYN finite code from the École Centrale Paris; - Modelization D: A cyclic isotropic compression calculation is performed in pure mechanics (equivalent to drained hydraulic conditions) as for Modelling A. The purpose of this Modelling is to test the possibility of taking into account mechanical properties that depend on the coordinates of the mesh in a nonlinear calculation with Hujeux's law. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry The test is performed on a single finite element isoparametric cubic \mathrm{CUB8} . The length of each edge is 1. The different facets of this cube are mesh cells groups named \mathrm{HAUT} , \mathrm{BAS} , \mathrm{DEVANT} , \mathrm{ARRIERE} , \mathrm{DROIT} and \mathrm{GAUCHE} . The mesh-cell group \mathit{SYM} also contains the mesh cells \mathrm{BAS} , \mathrm{DEVANT} and \mathrm{GAUCHE} groups; the mesh-cell group \mathrm{COTE} groups of mesh cells \mathrm{ARRIERE} and \mathrm{DROIT} . 1.2 Material properties The elastic properties are: - isotropic compressibility module: K=516200\mathrm{kPa} - shear module: \mu =238200\mathrm{kPa} The anelastic properties (Hujeux) are derived from the document provided by the École Centrale Paris: - power of non-linear elastic law: {n}_{e}=0.4 -  eta =24 - d=2.5 - b=0.2 - friction angle: \varphi =33° - Dilatance angle: \psi =33° - critical pressure: {P}_{\mathit{c0}}=-1000\mathit{kPa} - Reference pressure: {P}_{\mathrm{ref}}=-1000\mathrm{kPa} - elastic radius of isotropic mechanisms: {r}_{\mathrm{éla}}^{s}={10}^{-3} - elastic radius of deviatory mechanisms: {r}_{\mathrm{éla}}^{d}=5.{10}^{-3} - {a}_{\mathrm{mon}}={10}^{-4} - {a}_{\mathrm{cyc}}=0.008 - {c}_{\mathrm{mon}}=0.2 - {c}_{\mathrm{cyc}}=0.1 - {r}_{\mathrm{hys}}=0.05 - {r}_{\mathrm{mon}}=0.9 - {x}_{m}=1 - 	ext{dila}=1 1.3 Boundary conditions and loads An isotropic compression test consists of imposing an equal variation in load on each side of the sample. In the model under consideration, the cubic element represents one eighth of the sample. The boundary conditions are therefore: - The symmetry conditions: - {u}_{z}=0 on mesh cell \mathrm{BAS} group - {u}_{x}=0 on mesh cell \mathrm{GAUCHE} group - {u}_{y}=0 on mesh cell \mathrm{DEVANT} group - The loading conditions: - {P}_{n}=1 on mesh cells \mathrm{COTE} and \mathrm{HAUT} groups The load is carried out in three phases: 1. isotropic compression loading between t=-10 and t=0 where the pressure on the mesh cells \mathrm{COTE} and \mathrm{HAUT} groups varies between p=-100\mathrm{kPa} and p=-300\mathrm{kPa} . 2. isotropic traction load between t=0 and t=10 , where pressure varies between p=-300\mathrm{kPa} and p=-100\mathrm{kPa} . 3. isotropic compression loading between t=10 and t=20 where pressure varies between p=-100\mathrm{kPa} and p=-340\mathrm{kPa} . 2 Results 2.1 Method of calculation The validation is performed by comparison with GEFDYN solutions provided by the École Centrale Paris. 2.2 Quantities and reference results The solutions are post-treated with point C , in terms of isotropic pressure, \varepsilon_{
u}^{p} plastic density deformation and isotropic monotones r_{\mathrm{iso}}^{m} and r_{\mathrm{iso}}^{c} cyclic hardening coefficients. 2.3 Uncertainties about the solution Digital solution (calculation code). 2.4 Bibliographical references Reference document GEFDYN, École Centrale Paris. Available at http://www.mssmat.ecp.fr/IMG/pdf/resp_loph40.pdf 3 Modelling A 3.1 Modelling characteristics A Modelling is three-dimensional and static nonlinear, 3D. The first step is to preconsolidate the sample to p=-300\mathrm{kPa} (the first phase of the calculation), which is 100 time step between t=-10 and t=0 . This phase involves the monotonous isotropic mechanism of Hujeux's law. The isotropic traction phase from p=-300\mathrm{kPa} to p=-100\mathrm{kPa} (2nd phase of the calculation) is conducted in 100 time step between t=0 and t=10 . In this second phase, the automatic subdivision of the time step is activated to manage non-convergence situations of local integration. This phase allows to process the passage between monotonous and cyclic isotropic mechanisms and then to follow the mixed hardening of the cyclic mechanism. The new isotropic compression phase from p=-100\mathrm{kPa} to p=-340\mathrm{kPa} (3rd calculation phase) takes place in 100 time step between t=10 and t=20 moments. The automatic subdivision of the time step is again activated to manage the passages of cyclic/cyclic and cyclic/monotone mechanisms. The new cyclic consolidation mechanism created follows a mixed nutring, and then when the mechanism is switched to monotonous, it isotropically collapses. 3.2 Tested quantities and results The solutions are calculated at point C and compared with GEFDYN references. They are given in terms of \varepsilon_{
u}^{p} plastic density deformation and ( r^{\mathrm{iso},m}_{\mathrm{ela}} + r^{m}_{\mathrm{iso}}) monotone isotropic hardening coefficients and ( r^{\mathrm{iso},c}_{\mathrm{ela}} + r^{c}_{\mathrm{iso}}) cyclic, and summarized in the following tables: \varepsilon_{
