v6.05.106 SSNS106 – Degradation of a reinforced concrete plate under various stresses with global laws GLRC_DM and DHRC v6.05.106 SSNS106 – Degradation of a reinforced concrete plate under various stresses with global laws GLRC_DM and DHRC Summary: This test validates the GLRC_DM reinforced concrete plate damage model (see R7.01.32) and the DHRC steel-concrete internal sliding and damage model (see R7.01.37) for various cyclic loads: traction/compression, alternating bending, shear in the plane, anticlastic bending and their combinations. The analyses are done in static (STAT_NON_LINE). The results are compared with those of multi-layer modelling, in which the steels of the reinforcing sheet are represented by elasticity and concrete by the ENDO_ISOT_BETON behavior model (see R7.01.04). This test can usefully serve as a starting point for setting the GLRC_DM model settings in the various loading situations that may occur in practice. To complete, two modellingss are processed with a kit between GLRC_DM behavior and elastoplastic behavior with isotropic hardening, to represent the appearance of residual deformations as expected in reality. The Modelling O tests the thermomechanical system. In this Modelling, it is verified that the two thermal expansion loads (homogeneous temperature in thickness and constant temperature gradient in thickness) lead to the same stress state as two simple mechanical loads: extension according to \mathrm{Ox} and bending around \mathrm{Oy} . The modellings H to J then L and M correspond to the modellings A to E for higher levels of stress. This allows the DHRC model to be validated, with a comparison with the GLRC_DM model. The N Modelling corresponds to an anticlastic bending case (corresponding to the shear in the bending plane). The S Modelling is elastic only and allows to check the behaviour of the element COQUE_SOLIDE, especially in shearing. 1 Reference problem 1.1 Geometry | e | | | --- | --- | Figure 1.1-a: géométrie de la plaqu