ion of the stresses due to the deformation imposed and the corrector shall be summated to obtain the total stress through the plate subjected to a unit deformation in transverse shear. Evolution of \sigma_{xz} local shear stress \gamma_{xz} transverse shear through plate thickness. Evolution of \sigma_{yz} local shear stress \gamma_{yz} transverse shear through plate thickness. When the Mindlin formulation is applied, the transverse shear stress is constant in pieces through the thickness of each layer of the plate. When the Touratier formulation is applied, the transverse shear stress varies sinusoidally by pieces through the thickness of each layer of the plate. 10 Summary of the results The results obtained by the calculation are very similar to those obtained from the bibliography. Moreover, the different theoretical equities between homogenised coefficients are perfectly verified by the calculation. 11 Bibliography VOLDOIRE F. A homogenous behaviour of perforated plates of steam generators Internal Note EDF R&D, 1993.

