v7.31.114 WTNV114 - Water flow over saturated porous medium v7.31.114 WTNV114 - Water flow over saturated porous medium Summary: The hydraulic behaviour of a saturated porous medium is studied. Nine modellings are performed: two two-dimensional modellings (modellings A and B) and seven three-dimensional modellings (modellings C, D, E, F, G, H, I). The distinction between modellings is in the constitutive law fluid (LIQU_SATU for modellings A, C, G, H, I and LIQU_GAZ_ATM for modellings B, D, E, F). This test consists of applying a water flow on the upper side of the model and studying the effect of this flux on the distribution of fluid pressure in the saturated medium. This is an evolutionary problem. The first eight models studied are 2D planes (HM_DPQ8) and 3D density (HM_HEXA20 or HM_PYRAM13) with linear behavior. The last model is HM-XFEM. The reference solution is one-dimensional because it depends only on vertical coordinate. 1 Reference problem The test case study examines the hydraulic behaviour of a saturated porous medium consisting of a single fluid: water in its liquid phase. It is used in the Modelling of HM in Code_Aster . The constitutive law of the associated fluid is based on the modellings type LIQU_SATU (modellings A and C) or LIQU_GAZ_ATM(modellings B and D). 1.1 Geometry Illustration 1: Geometry Contact details of (m) points: A(-0.5,-0.5) ; C(0.5,0.5) B(0.5,-0.5) ; D(-0.5,0.5) 1.2 Material properties | Liquid water | Volumetric mass ({\mathrm{kg.m}}^{-3}) V Dynamic fluid water (\mathrm{Pa.s}) 1/Compressibility ({\mathit{Pa}}^{-1}) | {10}^{3} 0.001 {K}_{e}=3.77{10}^{-9} | | --- | --- | --- | | Solid | Young's modulus drained E(\mathrm{Pa}) Poisson's ratio | 225{10}^{6} 0 | | Initial status | PorosityTemperature (K) Liquid pressure (\mathrm{Pa}) Steam pressure (\mathrm{Pa}) | 0.4 273 0 1 | | Constants | Perfect gas constant | 8.32 | | Homogenized coefficients | Homogenized density ({\mathrm{kg.m}}^{-3}) Isothermal sorption coefficient Biot coeffic